//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Height of Binary Tree
Given the root of a binary tree, find the maximum depth (height).
Note: Height = number of edges from root to deepest node.

Examples:

Input: root = [12, 8, 18, 5, 11]
Output: 2
Explanation: Longest path: 12 → 8 → 5 (2 edges)

    12
   /  \
  8   18
 / \
5  11

Input: root = [1, 2, 3, 4, N, 10, 5, N, N, N, N, 6, 7]
Output: 3
Explanation: Longest path: 1 → 2 → 4 → (null) or 1 → 3 → 10 → 6 (3 edges)

      1
     / \
    2   3
   /   / \
  4   10  5
       / \
      6   7

Constraints:
• 1 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 3104
• 0 ≤ node->data ≤ 105
